 > [!NOTE]
-> compact-ui overrides the registration of several built-in tools so it can
-> control their presentation. Actual execution is still delegated to Pi's
-> native tool implementations.
+> This local compatibility build keeps `read` owned by Pi or its tool provider
+> and changes only its rendering through Pi's `registerToolRenderer` API.
+> The other six built-in tools retain the upstream delegation behavior.
+
+## Local compatibility build
+
+Version `0.1.3-yoyo.1` is derived from the verified npm `pi-compact-ui@0.1.3`
+package for private use with Pi 1.6.0. It is not an upstream release and is not
+published to npm. The upstream package did not declare a license; this
+derivative does not add or change one.
+
+The existing compact group and saved UI preferences remain in use. A `read`
+call with a `paths` batch shows its file count. The expanded group retains
+the existing result-preview limits and settings. Tool definitions, parameters, and
+execution belong to the active `read` provider. Install the derived package
+through an isolated generation and preserve the original package setting for
+rollback; do not edit the global npm package in place.
